## Context

Child of tracker 0236 (session-trace economics audit). The study phases
1-4 are closed and phase 5's live arms run on their own clock (0245,
0315); the tracker's own deliverable — a `trace-doctor` skill modeled on
skill-doctor (survey scripts + interpretation + tickets out, never
auto-applies) — is owned by no child. This ticket assembles it from the
already-committed scripts, plus the two phase-4 adopt items the tracker
lists as unowned.

## Relevant files

- `skills/skill-doctor/SKILL.md` — the model to mirror (structure,
  never-auto-apply discipline, ticket-out flow)
- `scripts/trace-stats.py` — census, per-agent cost rows, six-way tool
  taxonomy (0292)
- `scripts/trace-hypotheses.py` — hypothesis statistics
- `scripts/trace-pr-join.py` — trace→PR outcome join (cache accumulates)
- `scripts/trace-compact-audit.py` — missed compact/clear detector
  (phase-4 adopt item #3: wire into the monthly run)
- `rules/workflow.md` — phase-4 adopt item #1: micro-turn discipline rule
- `docs/trace-hypotheses-2026-06.md`, `docs/trace-counterfactuals-2026-06.md`
  — the interpretation playbook the skill encodes

## Actions

1. Author `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md`: run the four committed scripts
   over the last-28-day corpus under `~/.claude/projects/`, interpret
   against the phase 3-4 playbook, emit a ranked recommendation report
   (shadow dollars, stated as such), file tickets for actionable
   findings; never auto-applies changes.
2. Wire `trace-compact-audit.py` into that run (adopt item #3).
3. Add the micro-turn discipline rule to `rules/workflow.md` (adopt
   item #1), one paragraph, sourced from the phase-4 report.
4. Regenerate the skills catalog (`make skills-catalog`).
5. Smoke-run the skill's mechanical part on the live corpus; the report
   lands in the PR body or docs/, not as tracked per-session data.
6. Append a note to tracker 0236: skill assembled; integration review
   then owns only the 0245/0315 loose ends.

## Test

- Extend the skills adherence surface: catalog drift
  (`make check-skills-drift`) stays green with the new skill; if a
  description-format test exists (`tests/test_skill_descriptions.py`),
  the new SKILL.md passes it.

## Invariants

- Zero LLM calls in committed scripts; no per-session trace content in
  tracked artifacts
- The skill only reports and files tickets — never edits skills/rules
  itself
- Existing scripts stay additive-only

## Exit criteria

- [ ] `skills/trace-doctor/SKILL.md` exists, catalog regenerated, drift
      check green
- [ ] compact-audit wired into the documented monthly run
- [ ] micro-turn rule added to `rules/workflow.md`
- [ ] Mechanical survey smoke-ran on the live corpus
- [ ] 0236 log updated
- [ ] `make check` passes
